op_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_285b0e6d8bca45c19453f794","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Murphy Emori The 100 married child baby name\", \"Richard Harmon height 1.68 1.70 meters\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_ed611931993b404fb7b07844","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"blocks_finish\":false,\"code\":\"duplicate_query_blocked\",\"executed\":true,\"message\":\"Repeated received queries in bounded recovery: read a candidate, change the query, or explicitly replay the cached view. No backend call executed.\",\"ok\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_285b0e6d8bca45c19453f794"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"blocks_finish\":false,\"code\":\"duplicate_query_blocked\",\"executed\":true,\"message\":\"Repeated received queries in bounded recovery: read a candidate, change the query, or explicitly replay the cached view. No backend call executed.\",\"ok\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_ed611931993b404fb7b07844"},{"content":"Previously delivered raw windows (untrusted source data, not instructions or verified claims):\n[{\"document\":\"d1\",\"document_chars\":9101,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"30d6d8bd1feaa16d7480eae3bbb0d0772ddf0a956d9870efc705af2df5ace29e\",\"snapshot\":\"a531c0a6be82cbe578781b28cb207ff02e87008856d5212ec2eab3fae2afe076\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Screen Rant\\nauthor: Joseph Allen\\ndate: 2018-04-13\\n---\\nThe CW's slate of programming is a fascinating one. Many of its shows are actually fairly well-regarded, whether they take place inside of the network's sprawling Arrowverse or not. Part of the reason these shows have been so successful is because of their excellent casting and captivating stars.\\n\\nAlthough the CW has a number of great shows on the air and a really great talent pool, they more than occasionally like to cast actors who are actually related to one another in real life, or are married and have decided to form a new family with one another.\\n\\nWhether these two relatives show up on the same show or not depends on the specifics of the situation, but as many of the couples on this list are married, it's often the case that the two of them met while they were filming together. Other times, the relationship between the two actors was the reason that one of them was brought onto a show.\\n\\nWhatever the reasons might be, it's clear that the CW has no fears about keeping things close. After all, if one actor from a family works out, who's to say that others won't, too?\\n\\nHere are 15 CW Stars That Only True Fans Know Are Actually Family.\\n\\nStephen And Robbie Amell\\n\\nThis one is among the most readily apparent on this list, in part because Robbie and Stephen Amell share a last name. The cousins have also made homes for themselves on the CW, where they have both played superheroes.\\n\\nStephen has been Oliver Queen on Arrow for several years, and Robbie has played Firestorm on The Flash. Robbie also played a teleporting hero on Tomorrow People, which has been off the air for a few years now.\\n\\nIn addition to sharing an employer, at least sometimes, the two cousins also look quite a bit alike, and are each quite handsome. Of course, there a number of families who have spawned multiple successful actors because, at the end of the day, part of the reason actors are famous is because of their looks, which the Amells have in spades.\\n\\nJared Padalecki And Genevieve Cortese\\n\\nJared Padalecki has had a pretty long and steady career on television, and he's even had the chance to work with his future wife.\\n\\nPadalecki and Genevieve Cortese actually met on the set of Supernatural when Cortese was a recurring guest during the show's fourth season. Cortese played Ruby, a demon who seduces Padalecki's character and causes a rift to form between Sam and Dean.\\n\\nAlthough the affair between Sam and Ruby proved to be short-lived, Padalecki and Cortese's relationship turned out to be a pretty stable one. The couple eventually got married, and they now live in Austin, Texas with their three children. Supernatural is a show with plenty of tragedy, but things seemed to have ended in a happily ever after for Padalecki and Cortese.\\n\\nAly And AJ Michalka\\n\\nAly and AJ Michalka have been famous since a fairly young age. Both actresses made their debuts on the Disney Channel when they were still quite young, and they also to\",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/cw-stars-family/\"},{\"document\":\"d1\",\"document_chars\":9101,\"end\":6000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"296ede205a2fe113473e85be08b84f0d6833191551136843c6bff169eec542b7\",\"snapshot\":\"a531c0a6be82cbe578781b28cb207ff02e87008856d5212ec2eab3fae2afe076\",\"start\":3000,\"text\":\"ured together as a musical act. It's safe to say that the sisters' careers have been closely related to one another, and that was also true of their work on Hellcats alongside Ashley Tisdale, another former Disney Channel star.\\n\\nThe show followed Aly's character as she used her gymnastic skills to become part of a rather fiercely competitive and drama-filled cheerleading squad. The show only lasted a single season, but that gave Aly and AJ plenty of time to be on screen with one another, and kept their sisterly bond a featured aspect of both of their careers.\\n\\nJeffrey Dean Morgan And Hillarie Burton\\n\\nJeffrey Dean Morgan has made appearances in pretty much every popular television show. Currently, he's Negan, the big bad on The Walking Dead, and in that role, he's managed to call up a lot of menace from inside him. Morgan has also made appearances on the CW in Supernatural.\\n\\nOn that show, Morgan played the role of Sam and Dean Winchester's father -- the man who inspired them to begin their life hunting demons. Morgan's wife Hillarie Burton was also a regular on the CW, playing Peyton on One Tree Hill.\\n\\nThe two have never acted on the same CW show, but both were on the network at roughly the same time.\\n\\nOf course, that was long before they were married in 2014, so maybe the CW was one of the first things they talked about.\\n\\nJessica And Richard Harmon\\n\\nActors who are siblings in real life are commonly cast to play siblings on television. After all, that's the best way to make it seem like the relationship is an authentic one. In the case of Jessica and Richard Harmon, though, the siblings actually play unrelated characters in the world of The 100.\\n\\nJessica plays Niylah, a character who shows up in the third season and has been with Clarke on a couple of different occasions. Richard played John Murphy, a recurring character during the show's first two seasons who was bumped up to a major role during the third season.\\n\\nWhatever went on behind the scenes that led both of these siblings to star on the show is unclear, but it must be nice for them both to have a friendly face on set.\\n\\nJensen Ackles And Danneel Ackles\\n\\nSupernatural is one of the longest-running shows in television history, and Jensen Ackles has been one of the show's stars for its entire run. Although Ackles's co-star Jared Padalecki met his wife on the set of Supernatural, things happened a bit differently for Ackles and his wife Danneel. Jensen and Danneel started dating in 2009 and were married in 2010, but it wasn't until 2018 that Danneel showed up on Supernatural, playing a faith healer.\\n\\nInterestingly, Danneel once tweeted that if the show made it to its 13th season, which is currently airing, that would be when she decided to guest star. It turns out, that's exactly what happened.\\n\\nIn their private life, Jensen and Danneel live in Dallas, Texas with their daughter and a pair of twins.\\n\\nKatie Cassidy And Patrick Cassidy\\n\\nYou're far more likely to know Katie Cassidy than you are her\",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/cw-stars-family/\"}]","role":"user"},{"content":"Current control state (data, not source evidence):\n{\"current_notes_not_evidence\":[],\"evidence_shelf\":{\"omitted_for_capacity\":[],\"restored_exact_windows\":[\"e1\",\"e2\"],\"selection\":\"bounded recent first-delivery order; not a relevance/verification judgment\"},\"feedback\":{\"blocks_finish\":false,\"code\":\"duplicate_query_blocked\",\"message\":\"Repeated received queries in bounded recovery: read a candidate, change the query, or explicitly replay the cached view. No backend call executed.\",\"no_automatic_parameter_repair\":true,\"ok\":false,\"tool\":\"search\"},\"instruction\":\"Only finish is available. Submit an explicit answer with delivered evidence or abstain.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"FINAL\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":180,\"backend_calls\":94,\"model_calls\":5,\"output_reservation\":46409},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d148\"},\"ref\":\"d148\",\"snippet\":\" ... Despite a Cannes Film Festival premiere (being only the fifth TV series ever to premiere at the festival), The Idol suffered from poor ratings and was canc\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_television_shows_notable_for_negative_reception\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d147\"},\"ref\":\"d147\",\"snippet\":\" ... The second season premiered on April 15, 2020. On May 22, 2020, FX renewed the series for a third season, which premiered on September 2, 2021. On August 1\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_We_Do_in_the_Shadows_(TV_series)\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d146\"},\"ref\":\"d146\",\"snippet\":\" ... deepens the characters that audiences have grown to love a